
# --- git-gate: media & archive payloads (LOCAL FEEDBACK ONLY) -------------
# This block only stops UNTRACKED files from being added by accident.
# It is NOT the gate and NOT enforcement: tracked files ignore .gitignore,
# and anyone can force-add. The real gate is the server-side required
# object-scan check (see the repo ruleset + tools/object-scan.sh).
# Video masters and page-video packages live in OSS / the masters registry,
# never in git. (Q-A, video-storage architecture 2026-11-23)
*.mp4
*.m4v
*.mov
*.mkv
*.webm
*.avi
*.wmv
*.flv
*.f4v
*.mpg
*.mpeg
*.m2ts
*.mts
*.3gp
*.3g2
*.ogv
*.vob
*.asf
*.rm
*.rmvb
*.divx
*.m3u8
*.mp3
*.wav
*.flac
*.aac
*.m4a
*.ogg
*.oga
*.opus
*.wma
*.aif
*.aiff
*.mid
*.midi
*.amr
*.au
*.weba
*.zip
*.7z
*.rar
*.tgz
